What is the key characteristic of Link-State Routing?
b: Each node has a complete view of the network topology
Which algorithm is used to compute the shortest path?
 b: Dijkstra's Algorithm
What type of packet is used to share network information?
 a: Link-State Packet (LSP)
What does a node do after receiving LSPs from all other nodes?
 b: It reconstructs the entire network topology
What happens after the Link-State algorithm terminates?
 a: Each node knows the complete least-cost path to all destinations
Second 5 Questions
How often do nodes broadcast Link-State Packets?
 b: At regular intervals or when the network changes
What best describes the forwarding table?
 b: It maps each destination to the next-hop node on the shortest path
Primary advantage over Distance Vector Routing?
 b: Faster convergence and no count-to-infinity problem
How does a node update D(v)?
 c: D(v) = min(D(v), D(w) + c(w,v))
What is the final output of Link-State algorithm?
 a: A complete routing table containing next-hop nodes
